From 2c5f42bd5d5550708ce572cb5ea1183e7e8d4b3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 18:47:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03136/11362] [outer-loop] fix CRITICALs from the adversarial
 review: use the AUTHORITATIVE scorer

The adversarial review (3-angle, commit 3d43256a3) caught that my per-level metric
was built from a DOC PARAPHRASE while the authoritative scorer sat unread in the
venv (arc_agi.scorecard, package arc-agi 0.9.8). Three CRITICALs fixed:

MF-2/MF-3 (eval): reimplemented formula was wrong on 3 counts -- real per-level
score is min((human/agent)^2*100, 115) (a 115 cap that REWARDS superhuman solves,
not min(ratio,1)^2); per-game aggregation is an INDEX-WEIGHTED MEAN over ALL the
game's levels (unsolved levels score 0 and drag it down -> solving MORE/DEEPER
levels is the real lever); missing/zero baseline scores 0.0, NOT 1.0 (my inverse
was a gameable hole). Fix: DRIVE the installed EnvironmentScoreCalculator exactly
as arc_agi/scorecard.py:474-491 does, so the gate cannot drift from the
leaderboard. lp85 (1 of 8 levels) now scores 2.0069 (was my buggy 0.7225); proven
rank-inversion the old formula produced is gone.

MF-1 (gate): validate_canonical_baseline hard-asserted the RETIRED total-actions
7760 control, so an efficiency-bearing (re-baselined) baseline FAILED the guard
and main() refused every submit before _verdict ran -- the efficiency path was
unreachable in production. Now metric-aware: efficiency baseline validates on
'efficiency present for every CORE game'; legacy total-actions baselines keep the
7760 cherry-pick guard.

SF-2 (gate): a treatment that emits no efficiency (broken eval) now HARD-FAILS
instead of silently falling back to the retired total-actions metric (which could
PASS a real regression).

SF-3 (gate): per-game non-inferiority (the CORE sum is lopsided -- lp85 ~100%; a
sum-only check let a dominant-game regression hide behind a tiny gain elsewhere).

Re-baselined with the corrected scorer: core_efficiency=2.0074. Gate main()
unblocked. 24 tests green. early-stop unaffected (the review confirmed it safe/off).

